Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Bound native test process errors and range listener
 backlog

Session cleanup encountered psutil 7.2.2 upstream #2854: proc_environ returns success with AccessDenied set, so CPython wraps it in SystemError. Recognize only that signature and access-denial cause while preserving unknown errors and later owned-process discovery. Extract discovery to a topical sibling to respect conftest line cap.

The range fixture threads handlers but retains backlog five for eight concurrent range connections. Reserve sixteen pending connections so a descheduled acceptor accommodates the full fanout without SYN retries. Keep original observer, resume, integrity and platform assertions.

Proof: canonical session regression RED 2 failed/5 passed; GREEN 8 passed including unknown-error controls and real owned/foreign process cleanup. Held-acceptor real TCP regression RED timeout; GREEN connects all eight. Whole pm consumer suite and both original incident files passed; scripts/check 20 checks passed. Darwin errno22 causation and native containing-main CI remain to verify before task acceptance.
